  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Regional Development Banks Trust Funds</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Among the Regional Development Banks, Irish Aid supports two Trust Funds, one each from Asian Development Bank and the African Development Bank. Contributions are made to the Ireland Trust Fund for Building Climate Change and Disaster Resilience in Small Island Developing States (SIDS). The Fund is managed by the Asian Development Bank and help increase SIDS&apos; resilience to disasters caused by natural hazards, and to the impacts of climate change. Support to Africa Climate Change Fund (ACCF) run by the African Development Bank supports African countries to build their resilience to the negative impacts of climate change and in transitioning to sustainable low-carbon growth.</narrative>
  </description>
